For the KTH7823 product utilizing a QFN-16L 3x3mm package,
it is mandatory to directly connect the TEST pin to the Ground
(GND).


Conversely, for the KTH7823 product with a SOP-8 4.9mm×6mm
package, the TEST pin should be left floating during operation.


The KTH7823 product is available in two package formats: QFN16L and SOP-8, with pin definitions as described above. Due
to the reduced pin count in the SOP-8 package, the number of
output signals is correspondingly reduced.


The KTH7823 offers a wide range of pin functionalities, including ABZ-encoded incremental output, Pulse Width Modulation
(PWM) output, as well as SSI and SPI communication capabilities.


