For calibration purposes, a streamlined approach involves positioning the sensor on a plane orthogonal to the axis of magnet rotation. Upon rotating the magnet, the sensor sequentially
intersects with radial and tangential magnetic fields. The magnetic field ratio _µ_ can be empirically determined by capturing
the maximum amplitude variations of the Hall signal along the
X and Y axes. Here, _B_ _r_ and _B_ _t_ represent the larger and smaller
amplitudes, respectively.


